{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-q2-expr-sql/fold-many-FG",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-PAR-1",
    "PAR-FOLD",
    "SQL-AGG-ORDER"
  ],
  "description": "PAR-FOLD and SQL-AGG-ORDER, missing variant: the feed order of a GROUP BY over 4096 groups without an index on g (earlier: 1164 groups summed 1, 2932 summed 0). Asks, for FG, one GetRows over SELECT g, Sum(d), First(id), Last(id) ... GROUP BY g (every group's sum with its first and last feed id; the middle id is then known), the sums grouped by value, and for g = 1, 151, 1000 and 4096 the single-group Sum with First/Last and the ids of the group's rows in scan order, and the first 40 ids of the whole table. Follow-up probe (round 2) for PAR-FOLD, SQL-AGG-ORDER; runs on a read-only open of fixture r-q2-expr-sql-fold through DAO.DBEngine.120. Each DAO statement is preceded by a marker (a DROP TABLE of a table that does not exist, which always fails), so DBEngine.Errors read after the statement shows that statement's own failure or the marker's, never an older one.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
